Z||000000||FieroSTETZ||09-02-99||10:19 PM||||Is there any way to interface the Fiero computer with a PC? My dad's friend has a Miata with a palmtop connected, and can do thing like time 0-60, set fuel mixtures, etc. I am a hardcore nerd, and my old Mazda 626 had a p200 w/ a lcd installed, so i can install a computer in a car. I was just wondering if I could interface my PC with the fiero computer, and what kind of things are available. BTW, I have an '86 SE 2M6 4spd. Manual
Z||000001||theogre||09-03-99||12:56 PM||||you can only read the Fiero ECM. You cannot control it or most other GM ECM units.
Z||000002||terryk||09-03-99||10:20 PM||||P4 and up (P6 and flash) can have stuff controlled. You can also down load code to the ECM to take over certain functions.<p>Not on the C3 (Fiero type). Too bad too.
Z||000003||CRAGAR||09-08-1999||04:28 PM||||What's the least expensive computer or diagnostic tool that you can purchase for the Fiero diagnostic interface connector?||||reg||
Z||000004||theogre||09-08-1999||05:59 PM||||AutoXray GM scanner scans all ECM functions.<P>It's about 150$us. If you can't find it in any of the stores. Eastwood has it for 180$us. <A HREF="http://WWW.eastwoodco.com" TARGET=_blank>WWW.eastwoodco.com</A> <P>The GM only unit inclueds tha cable. The unversal unit is 250 + 30 for each cable you want.||||reg||
Z||000005||Ozzy||09-09-1999||08:53 PM||||Try checking this page out...<P> <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/techno.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/techno.htm</A> <P>I have not had much of a chance to check it out but some interesting stuff.<P>Ozzy||||reg||
